        </zone>
        <zone h='56308' id='3' name='Landform type in Early Helladic Period' w='48068' x='982' y='5958' />
        <zone h='56192' id='4' name='Landform type in Middle Helladic Period (2)' w='49509' x='50688' y='5841' />
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='25234' id='5' type-v2='text' w='52718' x='7138' y='63201'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'>Early Helladic:</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'> dominance of hills and ridges&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'>Middle Helladic:</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'> more diverse landform use&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'>Implication:</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'> While hills remain the dominant landform in both periods, the relative importance of ridges decreases and other landform types, such as spurs and mounds, become more prominent. This suggests a broader and more varied use of the landscape in the Middle Helladic period.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
      </zones>
