        </zone>
        <zone h='61215' id='3' name='Relief level in Early Helladic Period (2)' w='47610' x='982' y='9813' />
        <zone h='62617' id='4' name='Relief level in Middle Helladic Period ' w='43353' x='52521' y='8995' />
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='29206' id='10' type-v2='text' w='52980' x='2816' y='72664'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Early Helladic:</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'> low-relief dominant</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Middle Helladic:</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'> high-relief dominant</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Implication:</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'> The distribution of relief levels shows a shift from a dominance of low-relief locations in the Early Helladic period to a greater emphasis on higher-relief settings in the Middle Helladic period.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>While low-relief areas remain significant, high-relief locations become the most prominent category in the Middle Helladic period, suggesting a change in site selection toward more elevated terrain.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
      </zones>
